DOCUMENT();

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context()->variables->add(A => "Real");

$ans1 = Formula("cot(A)");
$ans2 = Formula("csc(A)");

$ans4 = Formula("sin(A)");
$ans5 = Formula("cos(A)");
$ans6 = Formula("cos(A)");
$ans7 = Formula("sin^2(A)+cos^2(A)");
$ans8 = Formula("1");
$ans9 = Formula("sin^2A+cos^2A - 1");

BEGIN_PGML

Fill in the blanks below appropriately to obtain a proof for the expression

[``` (1 + \tan(A) + \sec(A) ) \cdot (1 + \cot(A)-\csc(A) ) = 2 ```]


*Proof:*

[``
\begin{aligned}
(1 + \tan(A) + \sec(A) ) \cdot (1 + \cot(A)-\csc(A) )  & = 1 + \cot(A) - \csc(A) \\
& \qquad + \tan(A) + \tan(A)\cot(A) - \tan(A)\csc(A) \\
& \qquad + \sec(A) + \sec(A)\cot(A) - \sec(A)\csc(A) 
\end{aligned}``]

[`` \phantom{(1 + \tan(A) + \sec(A) ) \cdot (1 + \cot(A)-\csc(A) )} = \tan(A) + ``] [_]{$ans1} [`` - \sec(A)\cdot ``] [_]{$ans2} [`` + \; 2 ``]

[`` \phantom{(1 + \tan(A) + \sec(A) ) \cdot (1 + \cot(A)-\csc(A) )} = ``] [_]{$ans4} [``/ \cos(A) + ``] [_]{$ans5}  [`` / \sin(A)  - 1 / ( \sin(A) \cdot ``] [_]{$ans6} [`` ) + \; 2 ``]

[`` \phantom{(1 + \tan(A) + \sec(A) ) \cdot (1 + \cot(A)-\csc(A) )} = ``] [_]{$ans7} [`` / \left ( \sin(A) \cdot \cos(A) \right ) -  ``] [_]{$ans8}  [`` / \left [  \sin(A) \cos(A)  \right ] + \; 2 ``]

[`` \phantom{(1 + \tan(A) + \sec(A) ) \cdot (1 + \cot(A)-\csc(A) )} = ``] [_]{$ans9}  [` / \left [  \sin(A) \cdot \cos(A) \right ] + \; 2 `]

[` \phantom{(1 + \tan(A) + \sec(A) ) \cdot (1 + \cot(A)-\csc(A) )} = 2 `]

_Your goal is to fill in the blanks with appropriate formulas to make adjacent expressions equal._

_There may be other ways to prove the original identity but this problem requires the correct logic using this approach._

Hint:  At each step, look to see which terms might cancel or combine.

END_PGML

ENDDOCUMENT();
